WEBVTT

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:53.460
Would you there be no rainbows and no strolling down?

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:03.000
BOO!

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:08.090
BOO!

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:08.230
BOO!

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:19.370
BOO!

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:13.150
Wasting time. She promised to be here at 2.30. It's now 32. I wonder where she can be.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:14.890
I'll have a look round, though.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.790
I say, just look at the state of my suit.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.610
Oh, I'm terribly sorry. Let me brush you up a bit.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.460
I say, don't do that.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:25.180
Oh, I'm awfully sorry. I'm terribly nervous today. I'm meeting a girl.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:38.630
Oh, I see. That girl's got it.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:40.590
Yes, and I've got that.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:41.740
Well, what's that?

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:42.580
That's it.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.330
Okay, old chap, go to it.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.370
You bet your life.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:47.780
Whoopee.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:49.840
Hello.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.240
I'm in quite a lot of weather lately, aren't we?

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.830
Oh, dear, there's so much I want to say to you.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:58.980
Oh, look into my eyes.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.490
Well, that's the one that's working.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.410
The hunk of cove men!

00:03:04.630 --> 00:03:11.020
Oh, baby! Oh, boy!

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:20.850
Well, I must say, you really put your heart and soul into that, Maureen.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:22.190
It's easy with Jimmy.

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:23.590
Don't make it too easy.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.480
Life is made up of wandering away from places that you love

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:43.160
Then when you're through with wandering one day

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:48.920
You wander to the place you're fond of

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:58.080
If I could take my pick, I'd pick Billy Piper

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.890
Hope I could settle down in one cold cold

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:10.550
I'd hang my heart on Main Street, London

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:15.220
For just a holiday I season

00:04:15.220 --> 00:04:18.520
In a sunnier cloud

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.230
Comes to home in

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.310
There's a place I wanna be

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.930
Where neighbor Mr. Eros

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:28.930
Can be dropping in for tea

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:29.970
If I

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:46.790
If I could take my pick, I'd pick Piccadilly, Piccadilly Retire, for just a holiday, I might spend season in a sunnier clime.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:59.600
When it comes to Holman, there's a place I wanna be, where neighbor Mr. E. Ross can be dropping in for tea, if I could take my pick, I'd pick.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:20.690
For an audience, Sally?

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:21.610
Yes, how about that?

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:22.950
Well, they applauded, didn't they?

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:23.810
All seven of them.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.150
I don't know where things are coming to. Saturday night, second house.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:34.660
Anyway, Rosa was in front.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:35.680
Rosa who?

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.680
Rosa Seats. Come on, this is our quick change.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.340
Business is bound to be slacking Oldham in July.

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:49.070
Why can't we play Blackpool in three weeks' time? You'll see a difference.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.190
Oh, doesn't look as if we will play Blackpool.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.630
Blimey, they didn't give us much of a chance, did they?

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.110
The show's only been running a month.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.050
Oh, well, there's no business like no business.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:05:59.550
You'll be late, Jimmy, darling.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.080
Well, if we are, you can keep them interested with a couple of numbers.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:15.360
Why does Mexie Jago have to have his offices so high up?

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:18.740
So he can call himself a top-slide agent.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.480
Well, let's get it over with.

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:23.530
How do I look?

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:24.760
All right.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:26.360
What's next?

00:06:26.870 --> 00:06:27.330
My head.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.200
Oh.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:36.820
Morning, Effie. Morning.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.680
Hello, everybody. Well, well.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:41.800
Knowles and Blake in person.

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:44.120
Hello, darling. I haven't seen you for ages. How are you?

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:46.980
I'm fine. I see you're still cluttering your act up with the old man here.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:48.920
Hello, Rigby. How's everything?

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:50.920
Oh, fine. We're booked up solid.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.260
We've had so many offers, we don't know which one to take.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.640
Yeah, I'm looking for work, too.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.180
Come, Sally, let's talk about something interesting, like me.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:06.700
my sweet no no what just that you can't see him you haven't got an appointment see you later then

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:20.060
darling and don't be late now good morning my sweet i haven't met since saturday this is a nice

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:25.020
surprise yes isn't it have you fixed yourself up with anything yet well nothing definite

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:29.980
i've been waiting an hour well i must rush now i'm having lunch with a film

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.420
He's putting me into a picture. Cinerama.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:37.120
That big wide screen. You'll really be able to spread yourself.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.320
Go on, try Maxie again.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.240
Okay. Effie, my darling.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:41.880
No.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.140
I want you to get on to Maxie.

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:43.680
No.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:45.160
I've got a proposition for him.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:45.480
No.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:46.840
Tell him there's a lot of money in it.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:52.350
Jimmy's got a proposition for you.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.470
He says there's a lot of money in it.

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:56.900
Money.

00:07:58.590 --> 00:07:59.690
Okay, you can go in.

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:01.460
Sal, we're in.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:07.570
Hey, look, I've been here for an hour.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:08.560
Be brief, Jimmy.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:10.680
Well, what's the proposition?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:11.920
Knowles and Blake.

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:12.820
We want some dates.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.990
Now, look, if that's all you came in here for...

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:17.390
Now, wait a minute. Hang on a minute, Max.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:18.490
You know we're a good act.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:19.460
So what?

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:21.860
So a couple thousand dollars.

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.660
What do you think I am, a magician?

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.360
Well, don't you know the whole business has gone to pot?

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:29.980
Only way you could...

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.840
At Villa Theatre nowadays is to take all your clothes off.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:34.800
Well, don't look at me. Or me.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.140
I suppose we're too late for that summer season at Grimsby.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:43.380
Mm-hmm. Too late. The show's opened already and closed.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.680
Sorry, there is nothing I can offer you. Nothing.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:49.920
Of course, if anything does come up, I'll let you know. Thanks.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:52.600
Just a minute, Jim. Max, how about TV?

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.700
Well, I thought Jimmy was dead against it. So I am.

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.490
Well, I reckon I wouldn't mind trying it once.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.840
It's great publicity, and you don't need talent.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:03.720
We have talent.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.900
Never mind. You could still be a success.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.670
Look at this one. Jerry Lomas.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:09.940
Now he's a national figure.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:13.130
He is making 500 a week. Crazy.

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:14.580
Disgraceful.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.620
I'm ashamed to take my 10%.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.320
What are our chances of getting on?

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.640
Well, they're just setting up a new big Saturday night show.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:21.220
A comedy?

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:21.560
Sure.

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:22.820
We'll do it.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.370
This'll be for you alone, Jimmy.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.360
They want comedy sketches.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:27.870
Wait a minute.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.000
Me?

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:29.970
On my...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:30.840
Uh-huh.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:31.980
No thanks.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:34.710
Jim, if there's no spot for me, then there's no spot.

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:35.870
It's only just this once.

00:09:36.110 --> 00:09:38.350
If you're interested, auditions are on Friday.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:39.330
I'll get your name on the list.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.020
Audition? Me?

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.080
Well, sure, they have to see what they're buying, don't they?

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:44.360
But surely they know my stuff.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:47.000
Of course, on this date, yes.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.460
But they want to see how it's going to come over on the screen.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:51.490
It's very small.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:53.710
I don't care how small it is.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.720
After 10 years on the boards, I'm not auditioning for anybody.

00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:59.390
And what's more, Nose and Blake stick together.

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.360
Come on, Sal. Let's get some fresh air.

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:13.280
I'll come right away. Don't do anything until I get there.

00:10:14.390 --> 00:10:15.010
Who was it, Jim?

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.800
I've got to go out. It's David.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:18.600
Who?

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:20.820
David. He's in trouble.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:21.800
In where?

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:22.780
Trouble.

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.100
What again? What's he done?

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:27.160
Oh, I don't know. He's in some club.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:28.940
Somewhat?

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:29.980
Club!

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.730
A club! Do you mind? This is a private conversation.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:44.970
She says to him, I wonder who that should be.

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:53.710
I'll be with you.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:57.900
Please, have another drink. Come back, sir. Don't go.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:04.680
My song, you know, song out there.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:05.720
Very nice indeed.

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:11.270
But, uh, nobody plays my tunes like I play them.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.170
Nobody sings them like my wife.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.910
Oh, I didn't know you were still married.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:19.340
Successful.

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.100
Composer, not husband.

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.810
Wife, very successful.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:27.220
Singer, not wife.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:29.980
I hit the...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:40.180
she hits the road. That's how it goes. That's not how that's supposed to be. An E-flat major 7th.

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:47.400
Look at it. It's in the news. It's in the news. I don't care. Now be a good boy and have a cigarette.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:51.490
Come on. He's ruining my business, Mr. Knowles. Time was when I like to have him around.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:54.830
He's got class and people remember what he used to be. But who wants a drunk?

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.290
All right, I'll get him out of here. There's a little matter of a bill, you understand?

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.960
Oh, so that's why you phoned me.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.780
How much?

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:01.700
Twenty-three pounds.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:03.100
Twenty-three pounds?

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:04.240
What's he been drinking?

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:04.680
Urane?

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:08.650
David Moore's will now entertain.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:09.720
Careful, Dave.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:12.150
Jimmy, boy.

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.070
Nice to see you.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.190
Looking so well, too.

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:18.610
I'm not so well.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:21.920
Still, got to stand on your own two feet, huh?

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:23.420
Still, you won't take it easy.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:24.710
Put yourself together.

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:25.810
All right, I'll take care of this.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:26.730
What about the bill, Mr. Knowles?

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:27.610
Oh, yes, the money.

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:28.710
Twenty-three pounds.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:29.450
Get me a drink!

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:32.780
Yvonne's been with him all the evening.

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:34.400
Well, what am I supposed to do about that?

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.480
Ten pounds of meat.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:36.600
Ten smackers?

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.310
I can't afford it.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:40.550
That's all right. Forget it.

00:12:40.790 --> 00:12:41.170
What do you mean?

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.780
It's like a breath of fresh air to talk to someone with class in this joint.

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:46.120
Pleasure's mine.

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:47.300
You can clear off if you don't like it.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:48.860
That's another pleasure that's gonna be mine.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:50.920
Come on. I'll have to get him into a taxi.

00:12:51.260 --> 00:12:52.480
Come on, Dave. Come on. Pull yourself.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:53.240
Where are you on?

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:54.360
We'll go to another jet drink.

00:12:54.700 --> 00:12:55.880
I'll get you home. Come on.

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:57.560
Oh, it's all right.

00:12:58.360 --> 00:12:59.120
Writing any songs?

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:03.640
Oh, yeah. I write them. Nobody sings them.

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:05.820
Well, why don't you go back and sing them yourself?

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:06.780
No, thanks.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.320
One singer in the family's enough.

00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:12.250
Or, should I say, ex-family.

00:13:15.010 --> 00:13:15.790
What's the matter with you?

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:17.330
Just because your marriage broke up

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.870
doesn't mean to say you have to go to pieces?

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:20.350
I haven't gone to pieces.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:22.210
I'm just living the way I want to.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:25.300
Just as Anne is living the way she always wanted.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:29.970
Big star, luxury apartment, lots of...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.700
of rich playboys hanging around.

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:35.370
You know, Jim, I read in Variety the other day

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.930
where she's getting a thousand a week in cabaret.

00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:38.590
How about that?

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:39.910
That's wonderful.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:44.050
She wanted the bright lights, I wanted a home.

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:46.950
Or a bottle of scotch as a substitute.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:51.180
So they parted and lived happily ever after.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.680
Fine, that's fine.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:13:54.640
But how about your daughter Peggy?

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:55.500
Peggy?

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.740
She's all right, I imagine.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.940
Goes to boarding school.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:03.940
I get to see her a couple of months in the summer.

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:06.800
Come on, take things easy.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:07.760
Come on, give me the cup.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:10.480
Take it easy.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:11.660
Try and get some sleep, Dave.

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:12.220
Beat.

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:14.860
Well, I better be getting back to sell.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:15.990
So long, Dave.

00:14:17.190 --> 00:14:17.430
Okay.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.740
Jim, thanks a lot.

00:14:23.050 --> 00:14:26.060
But next time, I wouldn't bother.

00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:29.070
There isn't going to be any next time.

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:34.010
Oh, by the way, I had to fork out 23 quid to get you out of that dump.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:36.790
If you could let me have you back sometime, Dave.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:37.910
No hurry.

00:14:39.150 --> 00:14:41.850
Jim, I'm broke.

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:43.710
Cleaned out.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:46.190
What about all that money your dad left you?

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.320
Don't you know they slay for 40 years on the boards to save that?

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:53.510
Have you gone through the lot?

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:55.430
What about that theater at Felham?

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:58.420
Closed since 1940.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.990
I'm hoping to make a sale, though I'll pay you back out of that.

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:06.650
I hope so, Dave.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:10.440
Otherwise, I'm up the proverbial creek without a paddle.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:12.160
So long, old boy.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:18.610
23 quid.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.240
Why didn't you give him the lot while you were about it?

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:24.100
I couldn't let him get pinched, could I?

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:26.250
We'll get it back as soon as he sells the theatre.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:27.140
What theatre?

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:29.860
Oh, his mum and dad left him this theatre at Fellham.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:31.080
I'm not worrying, Sally.

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:32.280
Oh, no, I know you're not.

00:15:32.420 --> 00:15:33.720
Me, I'm the one that does the worrying.

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:35.040
I have to find the rent.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.060
I have to buy the food.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.600
Oh, don't start that again.

00:15:37.880 --> 00:15:39.860
Shut up in this dreary flat night after night

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.640
while you go out throwing your money around

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:43.100
like a Rothschild with six arms.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:44.380
Scraping and screwing.

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:45.800
Scraping and screwing to make ends meet

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:46.820
and keep a roof over our heads.

00:15:47.020 --> 00:15:47.880
Watching every penny.

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.360
Watching every penny just so you can go

00:15:49.360 --> 00:15:50.980
and frit it away amongst your low friends.

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:52.000
Fingers to the bone.

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:54.060
Working my fingers to the bone to save on the laundry bills

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.320
and keep this miserable hovel clean.

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:57.820
And for what, I ask you, what do I get in return?

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.120
Insults and ingratitude.

00:15:59.260 --> 00:15:59.980
Bloody but insults and...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.900
Stop pronting me. I'm fed up. I'm sick of it.

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.970
I tell you, this settles it. Settles what?

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:10.420
You're going on TV, Jimmy Knowles.

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:13.850
Me on TV? You'll not get me inside a television studio.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:14.970
Never, never, never.

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:19.960
Good morning, Jonathan. How are you, sir?

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:21.640
Hello, Corley. Where are the victims?

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:22.920
Right here. Oh.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:24.480
Ah, I see them.

00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:27.010
I'm Crawley Walters, producer of this epic.

00:16:27.110 --> 00:16:29.080
This is Knowles. Charming, charming.

00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:29.970
And you're...

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:30.500
Jimmy Knowles.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:31.000
That's right.

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:31.950
Well, never mind.

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.410
Now, this is only an audition.

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:34.230
Nothing to worry about.

00:16:34.330 --> 00:16:36.130
Dickie here has put up a rough set for you.

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:37.730
It's only a scratch job, of course.

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.310
Yes, it's very scratch.

00:16:40.660 --> 00:16:41.360
Still, you've done his best.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:42.100
Oh, he's done my best.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.680
He's done his best to make it look like a holiday can.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:44.720
Thank you.

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:46.600
Now, you just go ahead and do your stuff.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:47.020
You see?

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:49.420
It looks complicated, but it isn't really child's play.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:50.860
Now, I'll tell you what happens.

00:16:51.580 --> 00:16:52.720
I have two cameras on you.

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:54.500
Camera one and camera two.

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:55.600
One's on a wide-angle lens.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:56.680
Two's tracking in and out.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:57.780
Yes, tracking in and out all the time.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:58.500
I don't let that worry you.

00:16:58.500 --> 00:16:59.920
The red light on the side of the camera.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.400
And this little fellow goes blink, blink, blink.

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:03.500
And that tells you which camera we hope is transmitted.

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.040
There's two sound booms also tracking.

00:17:06.280 --> 00:17:07.240
Yes, but don't let that worry.

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.780
Pictures are transmitted to me up in my little glass box.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:10.420
Do you see it?

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:14.180
And my job is to try to sort them out, cutting from one to the other.

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:15.660
All the trouble we have sometimes, don't we, Dickie?

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:19.860
While Carl is doing that, I'll be giving you cue signals from the floor.

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:22.000
Yes, you'll find Dickie here popping up all over the place, but don't let that worry.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:23.660
When I do this, it's a direct cue.

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:24.480
When I do that, it's cut.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.180
And when I do that, don't do anything at all.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:27.260
Right? Got it?

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:28.780
No.

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:29.970
But don't let that...

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:30.450
Where are you?

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:31.650
Oh.

00:17:32.250 --> 00:17:32.890
It's very funny.

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:34.550
Yeah.

00:17:34.670 --> 00:17:35.950
Now, I'm going up at the control room.

00:17:36.110 --> 00:17:37.030
Don't do anything till I get there.

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:38.610
Don't beat me to it, will you?

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:40.090
Right.

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:41.070
Positions, everybody, please.

00:17:41.610 --> 00:17:42.890
Cecil, can we have some lights?

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:44.070
Oh, right.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:45.450
He doesn't mind all for going on the set, Mr. Knowles.

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:45.770
Right.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.450
Good luck, darling.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:49.660
That's all right.

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:51.800
Sit down, Mrs. Knowles, if you can find a chair.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.310
Don't be surprised if anything goes wrong.

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:57.470
I'm always surprised if anything goes right.

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:01.590
I have to watch this chap, he's a bit dim.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:03.720
Do you know all your cues?

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.420
Well, do your best, we've got a date.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:22.450
Now, this is comfy down holiday camp.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:24.500
I say, what are you lagging behind for?

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:31.600
Just like home, sweet home.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:33.070
Oh, come on.

00:18:33.230 --> 00:18:34.750
Get unpacked and let's get to bed.

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:35.130
Okay.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:35.790
You?

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:49.790
Nothing.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:50.930
All right, get unpacked.

00:18:51.010 --> 00:18:51.710
That's what I'm going to do.

