I tell you what, I might be able to find a spot for it.

00:24:48.350 --> 00:24:50.290
I can't promise anything, of course. I have to ask Jerry.

00:24:51.910 --> 00:24:52.190
Jerry?

00:24:52.410 --> 00:24:52.970
Jerry Lomas.

00:24:53.090 --> 00:24:53.910
He's the star of the show.

00:24:54.220 --> 00:24:55.400
Yes, he mightn't like the idea of it.

00:24:56.560 --> 00:24:57.560
Well, supposing he doesn't?

00:24:57.680 --> 00:24:57.840
Ooh!

00:24:59.170 --> 00:24:59.970
I mean, it, er...

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:01.680
It's his show, you know. He's the star.

00:25:02.780 --> 00:25:03.640
Is that so?

00:25:04.530 --> 00:25:06.650
Well, you tell Jerry Lomas what he can do with his show.

00:25:06.970 --> 00:25:07.910
Transmitter, master, and all.

00:25:09.710 --> 00:25:13.070
But don't let that worry you, if you see what I mean.

00:25:15.020 --> 00:25:16.710
It's Dicky.

00:25:24.290 --> 00:25:29.980
Come in. Charlie, have you said...

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:31.080
Oh, but why?

00:25:31.600 --> 00:25:31.900
Good.

00:25:32.340 --> 00:25:33.060
You're not going to.

00:25:33.180 --> 00:25:33.740
Hey, wait a minute.

00:25:34.000 --> 00:25:34.660
Call off the deal.

00:25:34.880 --> 00:25:35.420
What's their number?

00:25:35.520 --> 00:25:36.420
Hold it, hold it, hold it.

00:25:36.520 --> 00:25:39.160
You seem to forget the fact that I need that 15,000.

00:25:40.680 --> 00:25:41.740
15,000?

00:25:42.260 --> 00:25:43.600
Is that all you're getting for a theater?

00:25:43.900 --> 00:25:47.000
Well, it's not very big and there are one or two things need doing to it, they tell me.

00:25:47.140 --> 00:25:47.900
They tell you?

00:25:48.900 --> 00:25:50.020
Yeah, I haven't seen the place myself.

00:25:50.120 --> 00:25:51.440
The solicitors are handling it for me.

00:25:51.740 --> 00:25:53.780
You own a theater and you've never even seen it?

00:25:54.390 --> 00:25:55.490
What difference would it make?

00:25:56.090 --> 00:25:57.010
Who's buying it anyway?

00:25:57.780 --> 00:25:58.600
Grimes and Farrell.

00:25:58.830 --> 00:25:59.930
They're the biggest sharks in the business.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:05.000
they're the only ones who'd look at it i'll bet they are at 15 000 they can sell it for twice as

00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:10.630
much as they're to commercial tv let me talk to them what is this come on come on give me the

00:26:10.630 --> 00:26:21.680
number gerard double nine seventy yeah i'll teach them 15 000 have you gone crazy yes isn't it fun

00:26:29.140 --> 00:26:29.780
who's speaking

00:26:30.730 --> 00:26:32.810
Oh, yes, I'll put you through to Mr. Farrow at once.

00:26:34.360 --> 00:26:36.840
Hello. Farrow, yeah?

00:26:37.650 --> 00:26:39.950
This is Sally Knowles speaking on behalf of Mr. David Laws.

00:26:39.970 --> 00:26:41.030
Say, wait a minute, I...

00:26:41.850 --> 00:26:43.370
He says the theatre deal is off.

00:26:44.090 --> 00:26:49.180
Oh, but I don't understand. Did you say off?

00:26:49.630 --> 00:26:51.350
Mr. Laws is going into business for himself.

00:26:52.930 --> 00:26:56.160
That's right. He's opening a show there and appearing in it himself.

00:26:58.160 --> 00:26:59.620
So you see, boys, the deal's off.

00:27:00.990 --> 00:27:05.080
Never mind. We'll send you a couple of tickets for the opening night, if you can still afford them.

00:27:43.560 --> 00:27:45.120
James, we're going out for a ride.

00:27:45.260 --> 00:27:45.340
What?

00:27:45.850 --> 00:27:46.270
You hurt.

00:27:46.470 --> 00:27:46.630
Yeah.

00:27:47.810 --> 00:27:49.530
Listen, I'm in the middle of Miss Morse.

00:27:49.750 --> 00:27:51.150
Oh, you'll have to go without them.

00:27:51.250 --> 00:27:51.950
Here, this will keep you warm.

00:27:52.050 --> 00:27:52.890
What are you doing?

00:27:52.910 --> 00:27:53.950
I can't leave this.

00:27:54.130 --> 00:27:54.590
Come on.

00:27:55.040 --> 00:27:56.980
But I won't have a clean thing to wear.

00:27:57.300 --> 00:27:57.780
Never mind.

00:27:58.100 --> 00:27:58.640
Oh, very well.

00:27:58.700 --> 00:27:59.600
What's the matter with you?

00:28:00.120 --> 00:28:03.180
Well, didn't you want your own theatre to put on your own show?

00:28:03.320 --> 00:28:03.520
Yes.

00:28:04.080 --> 00:28:04.820
Well, then, come on.

00:28:04.960 --> 00:28:05.700
Well, hold on to this.

00:28:06.080 --> 00:28:07.780
Oh, now, look what you've done.

00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:09.280
Haven't you learned to dress yourself yet?

00:28:09.420 --> 00:28:11.060
Oh, hurry up. Come on, then. Get rid of it.

00:28:11.340 --> 00:28:12.440
Oh, try.

00:28:13.550 --> 00:28:14.370
Right, let's go.

00:28:14.650 --> 00:28:14.850
Yes.

00:28:23.540 --> 00:28:24.180
Business slack?

00:28:24.650 --> 00:28:26.250
Always is. It's done as a high street.

00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:27.880
That'll be four and six.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:31.620
Which end of the high street is the Majestic Theatre?

00:28:32.430 --> 00:28:33.030
Right off of it.

00:28:34.100 --> 00:28:39.110
Oh! Blimey!

00:28:39.680 --> 00:28:42.240
When your father called it the Majestic, he must have had a great sense of humour.

00:28:42.710 --> 00:28:44.350
He said it needed a couple of things going to it.

00:28:44.670 --> 00:28:46.070
Well, all it wants is a good coat of paint.

00:28:46.910 --> 00:28:47.910
Plus an A, a J and a C.

00:28:48.520 --> 00:28:50.460
The Mesty! That's unusual.

00:28:51.940 --> 00:28:53.280
It's easy to get an A, J and a C.

00:28:53.950 --> 00:28:55.790
Why don't you just get another S and call it the Mess?

00:28:58.080 --> 00:28:59.000
Let's have a look at the inside.

00:29:05.980 --> 00:29:08.900
I mean, there's only natural that the place would look run down after all these years.

00:29:13.520 --> 00:29:15.500
Say, Dave, uh, Dave, have you got the key?

00:29:15.940 --> 00:29:18.580
Oh, I forgot. The solicitor must have it.

00:29:18.820 --> 00:29:19.820
Oh, David.

00:29:20.460 --> 00:29:20.780
Sorry.

00:29:21.160 --> 00:29:23.240
Well, we may as well go back. We'll never get past this lot.

00:29:24.520 --> 00:29:29.420
This way for the one and nine.

00:29:32.100 --> 00:29:33.200
What are you doing down there?

00:29:33.790 --> 00:29:34.730
Getting up.

00:29:36.520 --> 00:29:46.120
Good-looking fellow, eh?

00:29:46.840 --> 00:29:48.200
You wouldn't think that was Dave's dad, would you?

00:29:49.340 --> 00:29:49.740
David?

00:29:56.380 --> 00:29:57.740
One thing, it's nice and light.

00:29:59.110 --> 00:29:59.970
It's a German system.

